# Pairs with ReadPositionHonest. The design that cold-starts a leaf whose
# snapshot failed to load whenever its WAL prefix is still intact (tail 0) at
# the moment of the probe. The leaf's pin was resolved against that snapshot
# and the pin store can never lower it, so the GC stays entitled to trim the
# covered prefix for the whole cold rebuild; it trims, and the rebuild reads
# from the new tail past the leaf's own acknowledged writes. A standing check
# that an instantaneous tail probe does not make the cold path safe (#4450).
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestLoadFailureColdStartsOverIntactWal
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a failed snapshot load cold-starts when the tail reads 0, and the GC trims under the leaf's old pin mid-rebuild
PERTURBS: ActivateLoadFail
--- FIND
    /\ snapCov[l] # NoSnap \/ SnapshotVanished(l)
    /\ UNCHANGED vars
--- REPLACE
    /\ snapCov[l] # NoSnap
\* MUTATION: cold start when the prefix probes intact.
    /\ tail = 0
    /\ up' = [up EXCEPT ![l] = TRUE]
    /\ replayRequested' = [replayRequested EXCEPT ![l] = TRUE]
    /\ cache' = [cache EXCEPT ![l] = {}]
    /\ rp' = [rp EXCEPT ![l] = -1]
    /\ stCp' = [stCp EXCEPT ![l] = durCp[l]]
    /\ anchor' = [anchor EXCEPT ![l] = durCp[l]]
    /\ UNCHANGED walVars
    /\ UNCHANGED <<durCp, clk, cov, snapCov, snapRows, stale>>
    /\ UNCHANGED pinVars
    /\ UNCHANGED faults
--- END
